alternative_question:
We're using Windows Identity Foundation (WIF) in our MVC 4 web application, along with an STS for authentication. So far, everything is working as expected. However, we've encountered an issue when logging in and then returning to the site. Our username is displayed correctly, and we can log out successfully. To secure API calls, we're utilizing a bootstrap token. The problem arises when we log in - the bootstrap token becomes null, despite claims being present. This behavior only occurs after the initial login; if we recycle the app pool or rebuild the site in Visual Studio, the token is correctly displayed.

Our current approach to obtaining the token involves the following code:

```csharp
var claimsPrincipal = (ClaimsPrincipal)System.Web.HttpContext.Current.User;
var bootstrapContext = (BootstrapContext)claimsPrincipal.Identities.First().BootstrapContext;

ViewBag.Token = bootstrapContext.Token;
```

Does anyone have insight on how to resolve this issue and retrieve the token without requiring an app pool recycle or site rebuild?

